{"id":"word:hebrew:H6403","type":"word","title":"פָּלַט","subtitle":"H6403 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to slip out, i.e. escape ; causatively, to deliver","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to פָּלַט (H6403) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 25 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"פָּלַט (pâlaṭ) means to slip out, i.e. escape ; causatively, to deliver First listed occurrence: 2Sam 22 2."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"פָּלַט","transliteration":"pâlaṭ","pronunciation":"paw-lat'","strong":"H6403","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6403","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וּ/מְפַלְטִ֣/י","וּ/מְפַלְטִ/י","וַֽ/תְּפַלְּטֵ֔/נִי","וּ/פָֽלְטוּ֙","וְ/יַפְלִ֖יט"],"morphs":[["HC/Vprmsc/Sp1cs",5],["HVpi2ms/Sp1cs",2],["HVpv2ms/Sp1cs",2],["HC/Vpw2ms/Sp1cs",1],["HC/Vqq3cp",1],["HC/Vhi3ms",1],["HVpi3fs",1],["HC/Vph1cs",1],["HVhi2ms",1],["HVpi2ms",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"to slip out, i.e. escape ; causatively, to deliver","usage":"calve, carry away safe, deliver, (cause to) escape.","full":"H6403. palat [ מָּלַט ] verb escape (Late Hebrew id. ; Phoenician in proper name; Arabic IV escape , Vulgar Arabic ; Old Aramaic פלט Pa`el rescue , מְּלַט ᵑ7 Syriac ); — Qal Perfect 3plural consecutive וּפָֽלְטוּ Ezek 7:16 and (if) escapers of them escape ). Pi`el causative: Imperfect 3masculine singular suffix יְפַלְּטֵם ; 2 masculine singular תְּפַלֵּט Micah 6:14 , etc.; Imperative masculine singular מַּלְּטָה Psa 17:13 , etc.; Participle suffix מְפַלְּטִי 18:3 +; — 1 bring into security Micah 6:14 ; especially of ׳י , deliver , with accusative of person, Psa 22:5 ; 22:9 ; 31:2 ; 37:40 ; 71:2 (+ הִצִיל ), 82:4 ; 91:14 ; + מִן from 2Sam 22:44 = Psa 18:44 ; 18:49 ( מוֺצִיא || 2Sam 22:49 ), 17:13 ; 2Sam 37:40; 2Sam 43:1; 2Sam 71:4; participle with suffix, my deliverer 22:2 = Psa 18:3 ; Psalm 40:18; Psalm 70:6; 144:2 . 2 cause to escape, cast forth , of cow calving Job 21:10 (compare [ מָלַט ] Hiph`il , also ᵑ7 vomit out, and so ). 3 apparently intransitive be delivered , with מִן Job 23:7 , but dubious; Bu Qal ('perhaps'); ᵐ5 Du read מִשְׁמָּטִי as object (but elsewhere ׳י subject of Pi`el ). Hiph`il bring into security; Imperfect 3masculine singular יַפְלִיט Isa 5:29 of Assyria, under figure of lion, carrying off prey (opposed to הִצִּיל ); 2 masculine singular תַּפְלִיט Micah 6:14 (compare Pi`el1. ).","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"2Sam 22 2","keyReferences":["2Sam 22 2","2Sam 22 44","Ezek 7 16","Isa 5 29","Job 21 10","Job 23 7","Mic 6 14","Mic 6 14"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":25,"occurrences":[{"reference":"2Sam 22 2","book":"2Sam","chapter":22,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/מְפַלְטִ/י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vprmsc/Sp1cs"},{"reference":"2Sam 22 44","book":"2Sam","chapter":22,"verse":44,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַֽ/תְּפַלְּטֵ֔/נִי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vpw2ms/Sp1cs"},{"reference":"Ezek 7 16","book":"Ezek","chapter":7,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/פָֽלְטוּ֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqq3cp"},{"reference":"Isa 5 29","book":"Isa","chapter":5,"verse":29,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/יַפְלִ֖יט","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhi3ms"},{"reference":"Job 21 10","book":"Job","chapter":21,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תְּפַלֵּ֥ט","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVpi3fs"},{"reference":"Job 23 7","book":"Job","chapter":23,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/אֲפַלְּטָ֥ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vph1cs"},{"reference":"Mic 6 14","book":"Mic","chapter":6,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תַפְלִ֔יט","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVhi2ms"},{"reference":"Mic 6 14","book":"Mic","chapter":6,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תְּפַלֵּ֖ט","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVpi2ms"},{"reference":"Ps 17 13